From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NuxFX contributors
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dzn: report the robust buffer access size alignments

VK_EXT_robustness2 has the driver report how far it rounds the range of a buffer descriptor
before it bounds-checks accesses (robustStorageBufferAccessSizeAlignment and
robustUniformBufferAccessSizeAlignment, powers of two from 1 to 256). dzn reported 0 for both,
which is not a valid value and told applications that ranges are checked exactly.

They are not: a constant buffer view is made with its size rounded up to 256 bytes (D3D12's
granularity) and a raw buffer view with its size rounded up to a dword. tests/robustness_test.c
shows it: with a uniform buffer descriptor of 64 bytes, a read at byte 64 returned the data of
the buffer instead of zero, while reads past 256 bytes returned zero. Storage buffers were
already exact at dword granularity.

Report 4 and 256. Accesses inside the rounded range are in bounds, which is what dzn does; the
ones past it read zero and write nothing, which the test now checks.
---
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
index 0f210f1..3654547 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
@@ -1019,6 +1019,12 @@
       .minMemoryMapAlignment = 64,
       .minTexelBufferOffsetAlignment = 32,
       .minUniformBufferOffsetAlignment = D3D12_CONSTANT_BUFFER_DATA_PLACEMENT_ALIGNMENT,
+      /* Buffer descriptors are rounded up when they are made: raw buffer views to a dword and
+       * constant buffer views to the 256-byte D3D12 granularity (dzn_descriptor_heap_write_buffer_desc
+       * and need_custom_buffer_descriptor). Accesses inside the rounded range are in bounds, the
+       * ones past it read zero and write nothing (VK_EXT_robustness2). */
+      .robustStorageBufferAccessSizeAlignment = 4,
+      .robustUniformBufferAccessSizeAlignment = 256,
       .minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment = D3D12_RAW_UAV_SRV_BYTE_ALIGNMENT,
       .minTexelOffset = D3D12_COMMONSHADER_TEXEL_OFFSET_MAX_NEGATIVE,
       .maxTexelOffset = D3D12_COMMONSHADER_TEXEL_OFFSET_MAX_POSITIVE,
